          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "собор (sobór) — \"a cathedral; a council\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Рядом с ратушей — большой собор. Ryádom s rátushey — bolshóy sobór. Next to the town hall there is a large cathedral."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. A big main church; also an assembly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "собор (sobór) came from Church Slavonic sŭborŭ 'a meeting, a council' (EtymDB), which is inherited from Proto-Slavic sŭborŭ 'a gathering', a noun usually linked with собирать 'to gather': first the gathering of the faithful, then their great church."
            }
          ]
        },
